  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Khao kluk kapi serves 4 and takes about 35 minutes. The dish has two main components: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "jasmine rice",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "jasmine-rice"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " fried with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "shrimp paste",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shrimp-paste"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", and a sweet caramelised pork topping made with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "palm sugar",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "palm-sugar"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "dark soy sauce",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "soy-sauce-dark"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Crispy shallots and lime finish the dish."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fry the shrimp paste in the oil before adding the rice. It will smell very strong at first. This is correct. The smell mellows into a deep savoury base once the rice is added."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
